ssifies EVERY ConfigError subclass as `config_unreadable` by isinstance, including InsecureUrlError (src/rebar/_config_schema.py) — which was explicitly designed to let a caller tell a deliberate cleartext-URL security-policy rejection apart from a malformed-config parse fault (bug bdb8). An MCP client branching on `config_unreadable` would mis-prompt the operator to 'fix an unreadable config' when the config parsed fine and was rejected by policy.\n\nProposed: classify InsecureUrlError before the ConfigError arm (a distinct code, e.g. `config_insecure_url`, added to KNOWN_ERROR_CODES), or exclude the subclass from step 4 and let it fall through to a deliberate code. Keep parity in docs/mcp-reference.md via scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py (the doc is generated). This is a behavioral classification choice — confirm the desired code name before implementing.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7d6a-16d2-ef8a-4b47","ticket_type":"task","title":"error_code_for: split InsecureUrlError out of config_unreadable","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["856cbfbf-599b-4fe2-8d5f-0575e848915a","73178f38-b625-4f01-abc9-9751f7f1625c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787393671816445001,"uuid":"623d187a-bc85-4cd1-984b-f3b04eabbb2a"}